      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When optimizing for a steady state, you're essentially trying to smooth out the pharmacokinetic curve of your existing medication. For bridging the afternoon dip, a targeted dose of 100-150mg of caffeine, taken about 3-4 hours into your study session, is a common starting point for synergy. If you notice a slight dip in alertness, a smaller top-up of 50mg later might help maintain the plateau. Remember, the goal is consistent output, not a sudden spike.",
